kept.description:
clove's /home/user/muhnschein/clove/ci/fuzz.sh `max_len_for` (lines 114-133) pins `-max_len` per target. It explains why: libFuzzer's default is the larger of 4096 and the biggest corpus file, and at that default a cap branch was unreachable ('that target's own PEX-cap assertion could not fail at any budget').

Sukkula's fuzz/README.md:109-110 says '`text_message` takes `-max_len=70000`, so that the 64 KiB cap is reachable'. The CI gate, scripts/fuzz-smoke.sh:64, passes no `-max_len`. The text_message seeds are at most 62 bytes and fuzz/corpus is empty in CI, so no generated input exceeds 4096 bytes. Lossy UTF-8 decoding can only grow that to about 12 KiB.

As a result, these assertions can never fail in CI, although SECURITY.md:181 counts them as CI-run S-rule checks:
- text_message's 64 KiB check (oracle.rs:144, via `message_violation`);
- command_json's 'over 64 KiB is refused as TooLarge' (command_json.rs:45-46);
- the same check in start_config.
